<!-- ======================================================================
     THE SCREENS THAT ONLY THE BAR USED TO REACH.

     WHY THESE EXIST AT ALL. The bar of applications above the screen is now
     the platform administrator's alone: for everybody else the left menu is
     the navigation, all of it. That is a better screen — one place to look
     instead of two — but only if everything somebody's job needs is ON it.
     These are the entries that were not, measured application by application
     before anything was hidden.

     NOTHING NEW IS BUILT HERE. Every one of these opens a screen that already
     existed and that the people gated to it could already reach; it simply had
     no door on this menu. Where a screen was already here it is NOT added
     again — "Channels (setup)" already answers for platform applications, so
     it keeps that job and only the two screens it merely borrowed move onto
     doors of their own.

     UNGATED IN XML, GATED BY THE HOOK. A `ref()` can only point at a row that
     exists when this file is read, and on a brand-new database the roles are
     created afterwards. So the gate is written in `hooks._gate_new_items`,
     which also SWITCHES OFF any entry whose screen is not on this database —
     an entry that opens nothing is a dead end, and this phase's whole promise
     is that there are none.

     `noupdate="1"` like every other row on this rail: once it is live, what
     somebody has since done to it is the truth.
     ====================================================================== -->
<odoo noupdate="1">

